  (null,2,187,'book-unlad','Unlad (Filipino Discipleship)','book','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📚 Book · Level 2 — Leader", "title": "Unlad — Filipino Discipleship Guide", "body": "<h3>About This Resource</h3>\n    <p><em>Unlad</em> (meaning \"growth\" or \"development\" in Filipino) is a contextualized discipleship guide for Filipino believers. Written to address the unique cultural dynamics of the Philippine church, it guides new leaders through the foundations of Christian growth in a relational, story-based format.</p>\n    <h3>Key Themes</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Salvation and assurance in a Filipino cultural framework</li>\n      <li>The Word, prayer, and fellowship as growth pillars</li>\n      <li>Overcoming \"bahala na\" fatalism with faith-based action</li>\n      <li>Family discipleship in the Filipino context</li>\n      <li>The EOLO (Each One Love One) evangelism mindset</li>\n      <li>Being a leader in barangay, school, and workplace</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Note</h3>\n    <p>Pastor — please provide more details on <em>Unlad</em> so this entry can be fully completed. Is this a church-published resource or an external publication?</p>", "footer": "[Please provide publisher and author details, Pastor]", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,188,'book-fresh-wind','Fresh Wind Fresh Fire','book','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📚 Book · Level 2 — Leader", "title": "Fresh Wind, Fresh Fire", "body": "<h3>About This Book</h3>\n    <p>Jim Cymbala''s memoir of the extraordinary revival at Brooklyn Tabernacle — sparked by returning to desperate, believing prayer. Transforms how leaders understand the role of the Holy Spirit in ministry.</p>\n    <h3>Key Themes</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>The primacy of prayer in church ministry</li>\n      <li>What genuine revival looks like at the ground level</li>\n      <li>Leading from a position of dependence, not competence</li>\n      <li>The power of a praying congregation</li>\n      <li>How God uses the broken and the ordinary</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Table of Contents</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>1. The Smell of Desperation</li>\n      <li>2. More Than We Can Handle</li>\n      <li>3. When God Shows Up</li>\n      <li>4. The Proof of the Pudding</li>\n      <li>5. A Taste of Fire</li>\n      <li>6. The God Who Breaks Through</li>\n      <li>7. What the Spirit Is Saying</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Application</h3>\n    <p>Assign to leaders before starting a new ministry season. Use as a discussion starter in leader huddles: \"What would ''fresh wind'' look like in our ministry right now?\"</p>", "footer": "Jim Cymbala · Zondervan", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,189,'book-master-plan','The Master Plan of Evangelism','book','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📚 Book · Level 2 — Leader", "title": "The Master Plan of Evangelism", "body": "<h3>About This Book</h3>\n    <p>Robert E. Coleman''s foundational study of Jesus'' evangelism and discipleship strategy. Demonstrates that Jesus'' primary method was not mass meetings but investing deeply in a few who would multiply.</p>\n    <h3>Key Themes</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Jesus'' 8-principle strategy: Selection, Association, Consecration, Impartation, Demonstration, Delegation, Supervision, Reproduction</li>\n      <li>Why depth with a few produces more than breadth with many</li>\n      <li>Evangelism as lifestyle, not program</li>\n      <li>The multiplication principle in disciple-making</li>\n      <li>Application for the local church</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Table of Contents</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>1. Selection</li><li>2. Association</li><li>3. Consecration</li>\n      <li>4. Impartation</li><li>5. Demonstration</li><li>6. Delegation</li>\n      <li>7. Supervision</li><li>8. Reproduction</li>\n    </ul>", "footer": "Robert E. Coleman · Revell · Over 3 million copies sold", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,190,'train-egr','EGR Evangelism Retreat','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Levels 1 & 2", "title": "EGR — Experiencing God Retreat (Redesigned as Evangelism Intake)", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The EGR is a two-day retreat experience, originally designed as a spiritual renewal event, now reimagined as the church''s primary evangelism and first-timer welcome program — the front door of the discipleship pipeline.</p>\n    <h3>Redesigned Purpose</h3>\n    <p>The new EGR is built to create a safe, engaging, and spiritually charged environment where unchurched friends brought by EOLO participants can encounter the gospel in a non-threatening, relational setting. Every EOLO invitation leads here.</p>\n    <h3>Two-Day Program Flow</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Day 1 Morning:</strong> Welcome, Icebreakers, \"Your Story\" sharing (participants share their life story, no gospel yet — just relationship)</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 1 Afternoon:</strong> Session 1 — \"Is There a God?\" (Creation, conscience, and the longing in every heart)</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 1 Evening:</strong> Session 2 — \"The Problem We All Share\" (Sin, separation, and the universal human experience)</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 2 Morning:</strong> Session 3 — \"The Answer We Didn''t Expect\" (The gospel presented clearly and warmly); Decision moment and prayer</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 2 Afternoon:</strong> \"What Now?\" — Next steps for new believers; Introduction to BTLI 101 and a personal discipler</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Follow-up</h3>\n    <p>Every EGR participant — believer or not — is assigned a personal follow-up contact within 48 hours of the retreat. New believers are immediately introduced to BTLI 101 and matched with a discipler.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Two-day retreat format · Quarterly recommended", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,191,'train-idc-basic','IDC Basic Discipleship Training','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Level 2 — Leader", "title": "IDC Basic Discipleship Training", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>IDC''s foundational discipleship training — designed for every believer who wants to know how to make a disciple. Practical, reproducible, and accessible to non-seminary-trained church members.</p>\n    <h3>Topics Covered</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>What a disciple is (and is not)</li>\n      <li>How to share the gospel simply and clearly</li>\n      <li>How to begin a discipleship relationship</li>\n      <li>Basic Bible study methods you can teach someone else</li>\n      <li>How to handle common questions new believers ask</li>\n      <li>The EOLO principle — Each One Love One</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Duration</h3>\n    <p>Typically a one-day (6–8 hour) intensive or 4 half-day sessions. Reproducible — graduates are expected to immediately use what they learn with one other person.</p>", "footer": "IDC · International Discipleship and Church Planting", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,192,'train-eolo','EOLO Campaign Orientation','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Level 2 — Leader", "title": "EOLO Campaign Orientation", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The EOLO (Each One Love One) Campaign is the church''s primary evangelism mobilization strategy. The orientation equips every church member — not just \"gifted evangelists\" — to befriend, invite, and introduce at least one person to the church and to Jesus during each campaign cycle.</p>\n    <h3>Orientation Content</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>The theology of \"each one\" — why evangelism belongs to every disciple</li>\n      <li>Identifying your EOLO person — who is your one?</li>\n      <li>Prayer strategies for your EOLO person</li>\n      <li>Natural conversation bridges to spiritual topics</li>\n      <li>How to make the EGR invitation</li>\n      <li>What to do when your EOLO person says yes — and when they say no</li>\n      <li>Celebrating wins — the culture of rejoicing over every soul</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Campaign Cycle</h3>\n    <p>Typically runs quarterly, aligned with EGR retreat dates. Every church member identifies one EOLO person, prays daily, and works toward bringing that person to the next EGR.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · EOLO Campaign · Each One Love One", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,193,'train-gifts','Gifts Discovery Workshop','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Level 2 — Leader", "title": "Spiritual Gifts Discovery Workshop", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>A half-day or full-day workshop combining biblical teaching on spiritual gifts with a guided discovery process — helping every participant identify their primary gift(s) and understand how they connect to ministry placement in the MULTIPLY pipeline.</p>\n    <h3>Workshop Flow</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Part 1: Biblical foundation — what spiritual gifts are and are not (1 Cor 12, Rom 12, Eph 4)</li>\n      <li>Part 2: The Spiritual Gifts Diagnostic — a custom 80-question assessment</li>\n      <li>Part 3: Interpreting your results — top 3 gifts and their ministry implications</li>\n      <li>Part 4: Confirmation circle — peers affirm what they observe in each other</li>\n      <li>Part 5: Ministry Placement Conversation — connecting gifts to specific ministry openings</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Outcome</h3>\n    <p>Every participant leaves with: (1) their top 3 identified spiritual gifts, (2) a ministry placement recommendation, and (3) a follow-up meeting scheduled with their Coach or Director.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Spiritual Gifts Discovery Workshop · Quarterly", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,194,'btli-102-103','BTLI 102 &amp; 103','lesson','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎓 BTLI Module · Level 2 — Leader", "title": "BTLI 102 & 103: Leading Others & Spiritual Formation", "body": "<h3>Course Overview</h3>\n    <p>BTLI 102 and 103 are the twin modules for the Leader level — one focused on the relational and leadership skills needed to lead a small group or ministry team, and the other on the spiritual formation that must underpin all leadership activity.</p>\n    <h3>BTLI 102: Leading Your First Team</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Session 1: The Leader''s Identity — Who You Are Before What You Do</li>\n      <li>Session 2: The Art of Facilitation — Making Everyone Feel Heard</li>\n      <li>Session 3: Casting Vision for Your Team</li>\n      <li>Session 4: Delegation That Develops People</li>\n      <li>Session 5: The Uncomfortable Conversation — Confronting in Love</li>\n      <li>Session 6: Evaluating Ministry Effectiveness</li>\n      <li>Session 7: Raising Up Your Replacement</li>\n      <li>Session 8: The MULTIPLY Review — Am I Ready for the Next Level?</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>BTLI 103: The Leader''s Inner Life</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Session 1: Spiritual Disciplines for Busy Leaders</li>\n      <li>Session 2: The Danger of Leading on Empty</li>\n      <li>Session 3: Temptation, Accountability, and the Secret Life</li>\n      <li>Session 4: Sabbath — The Leader''s Most Countercultural Practice</li>\n      <li>Session 5: Suffering, Trials, and the Formation of Character</li>\n      <li>Session 6: The Fruit of the Spirit as Leadership Competencies</li>\n      <li>Session 7: Marriage, Family, and Ministry Balance</li>\n      <li>Session 8: The Examined Life — Keeping Short Accounts with God</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Format</h3>\n    <p>Each module: 8 sessions of 90 minutes. Recommended to run 102 and 103 simultaneously in alternate weeks over one quarter.</p>", "footer": "BTLI · Bible Training and Leadership Institute · Your Church", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,195,'assess-gifts','Spiritual Gifts Diagnostic','assessment','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📋 Assessment · Level 2 — Leader", "title": "Spiritual Gifts Diagnostic", "body": "<h3>Purpose</h3>\n    <p>A comprehensive tool to help church members identify their primary spiritual gift(s) and understand how those gifts connect to specific ministry placements within the church''s MULTIPLY pipeline.</p>\n    <h3>Gifts Covered</h3>\n    <p>Based on the three primary spiritual gifts passages (Rom 12:6–8, 1 Cor 12:7–10, 28–30, Eph 4:11), the diagnostic assesses: Prophecy, Teaching, Exhortation, Leadership, Giving, Mercy, Administration, Evangelism, Pastor/Shepherd, Helps, Faith, Healing, Tongues/Interpretation, Discernment, Apostle.</p>\n    <h3>Assessment Format</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>80 situational and preference-based questions (rated 1–5)</li>\n      <li>Scoring produces a top-3 gift profile</li>\n      <li>Peer confirmation section: 5 people who know you well rate your gifts</li>\n      <li>Ministry match matrix: each gift is mapped to specific ministry opportunities</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Important Notes</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Results are a starting point for conversation, not a final verdict</li>\n      <li>Character must accompany gift — gift without character is disqualifying</li>\n      <li>All gift assessments reviewed by the person''s Coach before ministry placement</li>\n    </ul>", "footer": "Your Church · Spiritual Gifts Diagnostic · Custom Tool", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,196,'assess-salvation','Salvation Assurance Inventory','assessment','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📋 Assessment · Level 0 — New Believer", "title": "Salvation Assurance Diagnostic", "body": "<h3>Purpose</h3>\n    <p>This diagnostic tool is designed to help a disciple and their discipler ascertain with a high level of certainty whether genuine saving faith has occurred — or whether there are unresolved questions that need to be addressed before the person proceeds further in the pipeline.</p>\n    <h3>Why This Is Necessary</h3>\n    <p>In the Philippine church context, many people have been baptized, attend church regularly, and even serve — without ever having made a genuine personal commitment to Christ. This diagnostic creates a safe, non-threatening space to explore that question honestly.</p>\n    <h3>Diagnostic Areas</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Knowledge:</strong> Can the person articulate the gospel accurately? (Who Jesus is, what sin is, what Christ did, what response is required)</li>\n      <li><strong>Testimony:</strong> Is there a credible testimony of repentance and faith? (Not necessarily dramatic — but genuine)</li>\n      <li><strong>Fruit:</strong> Is there evidence of the Spirit''s work? (Changed desires, love for God''s Word, genuine love for others, awareness of sin)</li>\n      <li><strong>Assurance:</strong> Does the person have genuine assurance of salvation? (Not presumption, not uncertainty — but confident faith based on God''s promises)</li>\n      <li><strong>1 John Test:</strong> A guided walk through 1 John''s six tests of genuine faith</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Format</h3>\n    <p>Conducted as a one-on-one guided conversation with a trained discipler, not as a written exam. The discipler uses a structured set of open-ended questions. Duration: 60–90 minutes. Conducted before BTLI 101 and repeated at the Leader level transition.</p>\n    <h3>Outcomes</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Clear assurance:</strong> Proceed to BTLI 101 with confidence</li>\n      <li><strong>Genuine but uncertain:</strong> Additional sessions on assurance; use 1 John and Romans 8</li>\n      <li><strong>Unresolved:</strong> Present the gospel again; do not assume prior exposure = genuine response</li>\n    </ul>", "footer": "Your Church · Custom Diagnostic Tool · Confidential", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,197,'assess-leadership-readiness','Leadership Readiness Checklist','assessment','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📋 Assessment · Level 2 — Leader", "title": "Basic Leadership Readiness Checklist", "body": "<h3>Purpose</h3>\n    <p>A practical checklist used by a Coach or Pastor to evaluate whether a Team Member is ready to step into a Leader role. Prevents premature promotion and provides a clear, objective basis for the transition conversation.</p>\n    <h3>Checklist Categories</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Character (Gal 5:22–23):</strong> Is there consistent evidence of the Spirit''s fruit in daily life?</li>\n      <li><strong>Competence:</strong> Have BTLI 101 and 102 been completed? Is the person facilitating conversations well?</li>\n      <li><strong>Calling:</strong> Is there a genuine sense of God''s call toward leadership, affirmed by others?</li>\n      <li><strong>Commitment:</strong> Is the person consistently attending, tithing, and serving?</li>\n      <li><strong>Connection:</strong> Are they in healthy, accountable relationship with their discipler?</li>\n      <li><strong>Conversion:</strong> Has the Salvation Assurance Diagnostic been passed?</li>\n      <li><strong>Core Values:</strong> Can they articulate and demonstrate the church''s MULTIPLY values?</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Process</h3>\n    <p>Completed jointly by the person being evaluated and their Coach. Discrepancies between self-assessment and coach assessment become the content of a growth conversation. All 7 categories must be rated \"consistently demonstrated\" before promotion to Leader level.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Leadership Readiness Checklist · Confidential", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,198,'ref-character-love','Love','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,199,'ref-character-joy','Joy','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,200,'ref-character-patience','Patience','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,201,'ref-character-kindness','Kindness','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,202,'habit-accountability-pair','Weekly Accountability Pair','discipline','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,203,'habit-daily-devotional','Daily Devotional Journal','discipline','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🌿 Accountability · Levels 1 & 2", "title": "Daily Devotional Journal", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The daily devotional journal is the heartbeat of the MULTIPLY discipleship system. It is not merely a \"quiet time checklist\" — it is the primary place where a disciple encounters God in His Word and responds in writing.</p>\n    <h3>The Daily Practice</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Read:</strong> The day''s passage from the church devotional guide (15 min)</li>\n      <li><strong>Reflect:</strong> The devotional commentary from the guide (5 min)</li>\n      <li><strong>Respond:</strong> Journal entries answering the 3 daily prompts (10–15 min)\n        <ul>\n          <li>What is God saying to me in this passage?</li>\n          <li>What does it mean for my life today?</li>\n          <li>What specific action or attitude will I change?</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li><strong>Request:</strong> A prayer based on what was read (5 min)</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Accountability</h3>\n    <p>The journal is the primary tool for the monthly discipler meeting. The discipler reviews the previous month''s entries together with the disciple — celebrating growth, addressing gaps, and identifying patterns where God is consistently speaking.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Daily Devotional Journal · Printed guides available quarterly", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,204,'habit-eolo-checkin','EOLO Partner Check-in','discipline','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,205,'ref-character-led-one-person-to-christ','Led one person to Christ','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,206,'ref-character-completed-1-yr-discipleship','Completed 1-yr discipleship','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,207,'ref-character-active-small-group-member','Active small group member','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,208,'ref-competency-small-group-facilitation','Small group facilitation','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,209,'ref-competency-basic-biblical-teaching','Basic biblical teaching','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,210,'ref-competency-member-care','Member care','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,211,'ref-competency-evangelism-eolo','Evangelism (EOLO)','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,212,'ref-competency-delegation-basics','Delegation basics','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,213,'coach-bimonthly','Bi-monthly Coach Check-in','coaching','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,214,'coach-calling','Personal Calling Discernment','coaching','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,215,'lifedev-devotional','Daily Bible Reading + Journal','coaching','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🌱 Life Development · Levels 1 & 2", "title": "Daily Bible Reading + Journal", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>See <strong>Daily Devotional Journal</strong> and <strong>Daily Bible Reading Plan</strong> entries for full details. This Life Dev entry specifically highlights the combined practice as a holistic spiritual formation habit — not just reading for information but reading for transformation.</p>\n    <h3>The Transformation Goal</h3>\n    <p>The daily combination of Bible reading, devotional reflection, and journal writing is designed to produce the habit that Mac Lake calls \"learning the Word\" — the foundational competency of the Team Member level. Over time, this habit builds the inner reservoir from which all ministry flows.</p>\n    <h3>Tracking</h3>\n    <p>Tracked in the Accountability App and reviewed monthly with the discipler. Goal: 5+ days per week sustained for 3+ months before transitioning to the Leader level.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Daily Devotional System", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,2,216,'lifedev-accountability-app','Accountability App Tracking','coaching','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,217,'book-usad','Usad (Growth Guide)','book','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📚 Book · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "Usad — Filipino Growth Guide", "body": "<h3>About This Resource</h3>\n    <p><em>Usad</em> (meaning \"progress\" in Filipino) is a companion growth guide for new believers, following on from <em>Usbong</em>. It takes a slightly deeper dive into the spiritual disciplines and Christian living, helping the new disciple transition from survival to growth mode.</p>\n    <h3>Key Themes</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Deepening Bible study skills</li>\n      <li>Understanding spiritual gifts and calling</li>\n      <li>Getting involved in the local church body</li>\n      <li>The basics of stewardship — time, talent, treasure</li>\n      <li>Maintaining faith in Filipino family and social contexts</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Note</h3>\n    <p>Pastor — please provide author and publisher information for <em>Usad</em> to complete this entry.</p>", "footer": "[Please confirm author and publisher with Pastor]", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,218,'train-egr','EGR Evangelism Retreat','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Levels 1 & 2", "title": "EGR — Experiencing God Retreat (Redesigned as Evangelism Intake)", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The EGR is a two-day retreat experience, originally designed as a spiritual renewal event, now reimagined as the church''s primary evangelism and first-timer welcome program — the front door of the discipleship pipeline.</p>\n    <h3>Redesigned Purpose</h3>\n    <p>The new EGR is built to create a safe, engaging, and spiritually charged environment where unchurched friends brought by EOLO participants can encounter the gospel in a non-threatening, relational setting. Every EOLO invitation leads here.</p>\n    <h3>Two-Day Program Flow</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Day 1 Morning:</strong> Welcome, Icebreakers, \"Your Story\" sharing (participants share their life story, no gospel yet — just relationship)</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 1 Afternoon:</strong> Session 1 — \"Is There a God?\" (Creation, conscience, and the longing in every heart)</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 1 Evening:</strong> Session 2 — \"The Problem We All Share\" (Sin, separation, and the universal human experience)</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 2 Morning:</strong> Session 3 — \"The Answer We Didn''t Expect\" (The gospel presented clearly and warmly); Decision moment and prayer</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 2 Afternoon:</strong> \"What Now?\" — Next steps for new believers; Introduction to BTLI 101 and a personal discipler</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Follow-up</h3>\n    <p>Every EGR participant — believer or not — is assigned a personal follow-up contact within 48 hours of the retreat. New believers are immediately introduced to BTLI 101 and matched with a discipler.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Two-day retreat format · Quarterly recommended", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,219,'train-entering-formation','Entering Formation — Pipeline Orientation','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "Entering Formation — Pipeline Orientation", "body": "<h3>Purpose</h3>\n    <p>The on-ramp into formal discipleship formation. Where New Believers Orientation (now at L0) welcomes someone to the faith, this welcomes them to intentional self-leadership — and shows them the whole journey ahead.</p>\n    <h3>What It Covers</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>The target: Luke 6:40 — becoming like our Teacher</li>\n      <li>The character we''re forming: the fruit of the Spirit (Gal 5:22-23)</li>\n      <li>The FATS filter — Faithful, Available, Teachable, Selfless</li>\n      <li>How the pipeline works, and how BTLI begins here at L1</li>\n      <li>Their “My Path” — what readiness for the next level looks like</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>How to Use</h3>\n    <p>A short session (or two) run by the discipler as the disciple begins BTLI 101 — so no one walks the pipeline in the dark.</p>", "footer": "MULTIPLY Pipeline", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,220,'train-bible-reading','Daily Bible Reading Plan','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "Daily Bible Reading Plan", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The church''s published devotional guide and accompanying reading plan — the daily anchor of every disciple''s spiritual formation. Developed in-house and contextualized for the Filipino believer, with Philippine illustrations, Tagalog-English blend, and local application points.</p>\n    <h3>Structure</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Daily reading:</strong> A passage from the Old Testament, New Testament, and Psalms/Proverbs (using a through-the-Bible-in-a-year plan)</li>\n      <li><strong>Daily devotional:</strong> A 300-word reflection written by church leaders on a rotating basis</li>\n      <li><strong>Daily response:</strong> 3 journal prompts — What did God say? What does it mean for me? What will I do today?</li>\n      <li><strong>Weekly:</strong> A discussion question for Life Community groups</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Accountability</h3>\n    <p>Disciples bring their filled journal to their monthly one-on-one with their discipler. The devotional journal becomes the primary tool for accountability and growth tracking.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Published Devotional Guide · Distributed monthly/quarterly", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,221,'btli-101','BTLI 101','lesson','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎓 BTLI Module · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "BTLI 101: Foundations of Discipleship", "body": "<h3>Course Overview</h3>\n    <p>BTLI 101 is the entry-level module of the Bible Training and Leadership Institute. It provides every new church member with the theological and relational foundations for genuine Christian discipleship — the starting point of the entire MULTIPLY pipeline.</p>\n    <h3>Learning Objectives</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Articulate a clear and confident testimony of personal salvation</li>\n      <li>Understand the basics of assurance of salvation (1 John 5:13)</li>\n      <li>Establish daily Bible reading and journaling as a lifestyle</li>\n      <li>Understand the purpose and meaning of baptism and communion</li>\n      <li>Begin consistent attendance and participation in a Life Community</li>\n      <li>Make the first EOLO (Each One Love One) invitation</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Topics Covered</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Session 1: The Gospel — What You Believed and Why It Matters</li>\n      <li>Session 2: Assurance of Salvation — Knowing You Know</li>\n      <li>Session 3: The Bible — How to Read It Every Day</li>\n      <li>Session 4: Prayer — Talking with God Like He''s There</li>\n      <li>Session 5: The Church — Why You Can''t Follow Jesus Alone</li>\n      <li>Session 6: Baptism and Communion — The Ordinances Explained</li>\n      <li>Session 7: The Holy Spirit — Your Helper from Day One</li>\n      <li>Session 8: EOLO — Your First Assignment as a Disciple</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Format</h3>\n    <p>8 sessions of 90 minutes each. Can be done in small group (4–8 persons) with a trained facilitator, or as a 1-on-1 with a discipler. Written assignments and Scripture memory required for completion.</p>", "footer": "BTLI · Bible Training and Leadership Institute · Your Church", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,222,'assess-spiritual-disciplines','Spiritual Disciplines Inventory','assessment','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📋 Assessment · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "Spiritual Disciplines Inventory", "body": "<h3>Purpose</h3>\n    <p>Where L0''s assessments confirm salvation and readiness, this L1 tool measures whether the core disciplines are actually taking root — the honest formation check for a growing disciple.</p>\n    <h3>What It Measures</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Consistency of daily Bible reading and devotional journaling</li>\n      <li>Prayer life and Sabbath rhythm</li>\n      <li>Church and small-group participation</li>\n      <li>Giving, service, and witness habits</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>How to Use</h3>\n    <p>Self-assessed, then reviewed gently in the Monthly Discipler 1-on-1 — a mirror for growth, never a scorecard.</p>", "footer": "MULTIPLY Pipeline", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,223,'ref-character-love','Love','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,224,'ref-character-joy','Joy','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,225,'ref-character-peace','Peace','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,226,'ref-character-faithfulness','Faithfulness','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,227,'habit-daily-devotional','Daily Devotional + Journal','discipline','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🌿 Accountability · Levels 1 & 2", "title": "Daily Devotional Journal", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The daily devotional journal is the heartbeat of the MULTIPLY discipleship system. It is not merely a \"quiet time checklist\" — it is the primary place where a disciple encounters God in His Word and responds in writing.</p>\n    <h3>The Daily Practice</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Read:</strong> The day''s passage from the church devotional guide (15 min)</li>\n      <li><strong>Reflect:</strong> The devotional commentary from the guide (5 min)</li>\n      <li><strong>Respond:</strong> Journal entries answering the 3 daily prompts (10–15 min)\n        <ul>\n          <li>What is God saying to me in this passage?</li>\n          <li>What does it mean for my life today?</li>\n          <li>What specific action or attitude will I change?</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li><strong>Request:</strong> A prayer based on what was read (5 min)</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Accountability</h3>\n    <p>The journal is the primary tool for the monthly discipler meeting. The discipler reviews the previous month''s entries together with the disciple — celebrating growth, addressing gaps, and identifying patterns where God is consistently speaking.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Daily Devotional Journal · Printed guides available quarterly", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,228,'habit-weekly-church','Weekly Church Attendance','discipline','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,229,'habit-eolo-invite','EOLO Invitation Habit','discipline','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🌿 Accountability · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "EOLO Invitation Habit", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The EOLO (Each One Love One) invitation habit is the practical evangelism discipline built into every Team Member''s daily life. It transforms evangelism from a program you attend to a posture you live.</p>\n    <h3>The Weekly Practice</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Pray:</strong> Daily prayer for your EOLO person by name (2 min)</li>\n      <li><strong>Connect:</strong> At least one intentional act of friendship/love toward your EOLO person each week</li>\n      <li><strong>Invite:</strong> When the time is right, invite your EOLO person to a church event, LC meeting, or EGR retreat</li>\n      <li><strong>Report:</strong> Share an update on your EOLO person with your discipler monthly</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>The EOLO Person</h3>\n    <p>Your \"one\" — the specific person in your life whom you are believing God to reach. Not a category (\"my coworkers\") but a person with a name. You carry them in prayer, build relationship, and look for natural opportunities to share your story and the gospel.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · EOLO Campaign · Each One Love One", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,230,'ref-character-completed-btli-101','Completed BTLI 101','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,231,'ref-character-90-day-devotional-streak','90-day devotional streak','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,232,'ref-character-discipling-my-eolo-one','Discipling my EOLO one','character','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,233,'ref-competency-personal-bible-study','Personal Bible study','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,234,'ref-competency-basic-prayer-disciplines','Basic prayer disciplines','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,235,'ref-competency-sharing-personal-testimony','Sharing personal testimony','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,236,'ref-competency-serving-on-a-team','Serving on a team','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,237,'ref-competency-financial-stewardship-basics','Financial stewardship basics','competency','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,238,'coach-discipler','Monthly Discipler 1-on-1','coaching','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🧭 Coaching · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "Monthly Discipler One-on-One", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The most important meeting in the MULTIPLY pipeline for new disciples. A personal, relational, 60–90 minute monthly meeting between the Team Member and their assigned discipler — the primary vehicle for growth, accountability, and care at the foundational level.</p>\n    <h3>Meeting Structure</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Connect (10 min):</strong> How are you really? Life update — work, family, health</li>\n      <li><strong>Celebrate (10 min):</strong> What wins — big or small — happened this month?</li>\n      <li><strong>Journal Review (20 min):</strong> Walk through 3–5 entries from this month''s devotional journal. What is God saying? Where is He calling you to change?</li>\n      <li><strong>EOLO Update (10 min):</strong> How is your one person? What happened? What''s next?</li>\n      <li><strong>Growth Challenge (10 min):</strong> One specific assignment or challenge for next month</li>\n      <li><strong>Prayer (10 min):</strong> Pray together — for the disciple''s specific needs and for their EOLO person</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Discipler Mindset</h3>\n    <p>The discipler is not a teacher at a whiteboard — they are a friend on the journey. They listen more than they speak, ask more than they tell, and always point back to what God is already doing in the disciple''s life.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Monthly Discipler Meeting · The Heart of the Pipeline", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,239,'coach-egr-followup','EGR Follow-up Care','coaching','manual',false,true,'{}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,240,'lifedev-devotional','Church Devotional Guide (daily)','coaching','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🌱 Life Development · Levels 1 & 2", "title": "Daily Bible Reading + Journal", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>See <strong>Daily Devotional Journal</strong> and <strong>Daily Bible Reading Plan</strong> entries for full details. This Life Dev entry specifically highlights the combined practice as a holistic spiritual formation habit — not just reading for information but reading for transformation.</p>\n    <h3>The Transformation Goal</h3>\n    <p>The daily combination of Bible reading, devotional reflection, and journal writing is designed to produce the habit that Mac Lake calls \"learning the Word\" — the foundational competency of the Team Member level. Over time, this habit builds the inner reservoir from which all ministry flows.</p>\n    <h3>Tracking</h3>\n    <p>Tracked in the Accountability App and reviewed monthly with the discipler. Goal: 5+ days per week sustained for 3+ months before transitioning to the Leader level.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Daily Devotional System", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,241,'lifedev-salvation-journal','Salvation Journal','coaching','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🌱 Life Development · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "Salvation Journal", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>A simple, guided journal completed in the first 30 days of a new believer''s life in Christ — capturing their testimony, their first experiences with God, and their earliest prayers. Becomes a precious record of the beginning of their walk with Jesus.</p>\n    <h3>Journal Sections</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>My life before Christ — in my own words</li>\n      <li>The day/moment I said yes to Jesus</li>\n      <li>My first prayer as a believer</li>\n      <li>The first Bible verse that spoke to me</li>\n      <li>What I''m most grateful for</li>\n      <li>What I''m most afraid of as a new believer</li>\n      <li>A letter to my future self, one year from now</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Purpose</h3>\n    <p>In moments of doubt or difficulty, new believers can return to this journal as a concrete reminder of what God did in their life. Also used in the Salvation Assurance Diagnostic as supporting evidence of genuine conversion.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · New Believer Welcome Kit", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,1,242,'lifedev-first-steps','First Steps Plan w/ Discipler','coaching','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🌱 Life Development · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "First Steps Plan with Discipler", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>A simple, written 3-month plan created collaboratively by the new believer and their discipler in the first meeting — setting a clear, achievable trajectory for the first quarter of the discipleship journey.</p>\n    <h3>Plan Components</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Spiritual habits:</strong> Which specific habits will we build this quarter? (Bible reading, journaling, prayer, attendance)</li>\n      <li><strong>BTLI 101:</strong> When does it start? Who is in the group?</li>\n      <li><strong>EOLO:</strong> Who is your one person? What''s the first step with them this month?</li>\n      <li><strong>Ministry:</strong> Where will you start serving? (Even simple: events crew, greeter)</li>\n      <li><strong>Baptism:</strong> Is this scheduled? What''s the date?</li>\n      <li><strong>Monthly meeting dates:</strong> Scheduled for the full quarter before we leave today</li>\n    </ul>", "footer": "Your Church · First Steps Plan · Created in Meeting 1 with Discipler", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,0,243,'book-real-life-discipleship','Real-Life Discipleship (Putman)','book','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📚 Book · Level 0 — New Believer", "title": "Real-Life Discipleship", "body": "<h3>About This Book</h3>\n    <p>Jim Putman''s practical framework for making disciples who make disciples. Its five stages of growth — spiritually dead, infant, child, young adult, parent — map closely onto this pipeline, planting the multiplication vision in the new believer from the very start.</p>\n    <h3>Key Themes</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>The five stages of a disciple''s growth</li>\n      <li>Discipleship as relationship, not just a program</li>\n      <li>The role of intentional leaders and small groups</li>\n      <li>How every believer moves toward becoming a spiritual “parent”</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>How to Use</h3>\n    <p>The primary new-believer book at L0 (stage 0B). Read with the EOLO Spiritual Friend to give both assurance and a clear picture of where the journey leads.</p>", "footer": "Jim Putman · NavPress", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,0,244,'book-usbong','Usbong (Filipino Devotional)','book','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📚 Book · Level 0 — New Believer", "title": "Usbong — Filipino New Believer Devotional", "body": "<h3>About This Resource</h3>\n    <p><em>Usbong</em> (meaning \"sprout\" or \"budding growth\" in Filipino) is a devotional guide written for new Filipino believers taking their first steps in faith. It meets them where they are — in Tagalog-rich language and familiar cultural stories — and leads them gently into daily Bible engagement.</p>\n    <h3>Key Themes</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Who God is — foundational theology in simple language</li>\n      <li>What it means to be \"born again\" in Filipino context</li>\n      <li>Daily prayer, Bible reading, and journaling habits</li>\n      <li>Dealing with family pressure and cultural expectations as a new believer</li>\n      <li>First steps in sharing faith with loved ones</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Note</h3>\n    <p>Pastor — please provide author and publisher information for <em>Usbong</em> to complete this entry. Is this published by your church or by an external ministry?</p>", "footer": "[Please confirm author and publisher with Pastor]", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,0,245,'train-egr','EGR — Experiencing God Retreat','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Levels 1 & 2", "title": "EGR — Experiencing God Retreat (Redesigned as Evangelism Intake)", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The EGR is a two-day retreat experience, originally designed as a spiritual renewal event, now reimagined as the church''s primary evangelism and first-timer welcome program — the front door of the discipleship pipeline.</p>\n    <h3>Redesigned Purpose</h3>\n    <p>The new EGR is built to create a safe, engaging, and spiritually charged environment where unchurched friends brought by EOLO participants can encounter the gospel in a non-threatening, relational setting. Every EOLO invitation leads here.</p>\n    <h3>Two-Day Program Flow</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Day 1 Morning:</strong> Welcome, Icebreakers, \"Your Story\" sharing (participants share their life story, no gospel yet — just relationship)</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 1 Afternoon:</strong> Session 1 — \"Is There a God?\" (Creation, conscience, and the longing in every heart)</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 1 Evening:</strong> Session 2 — \"The Problem We All Share\" (Sin, separation, and the universal human experience)</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 2 Morning:</strong> Session 3 — \"The Answer We Didn''t Expect\" (The gospel presented clearly and warmly); Decision moment and prayer</li>\n      <li><strong>Day 2 Afternoon:</strong> \"What Now?\" — Next steps for new believers; Introduction to BTLI 101 and a personal discipler</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Follow-up</h3>\n    <p>Every EGR participant — believer or not — is assigned a personal follow-up contact within 48 hours of the retreat. New believers are immediately introduced to BTLI 101 and matched with a discipler.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Two-day retreat format · Quarterly recommended", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,0,246,'train-new-believers','New Believers Orientation','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Level 0 — New Believer", "title": "New Believers Orientation", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>A 4-session welcome track for anyone who has recently made a decision to follow Christ — whether through the EGR, a Sunday service, or personal evangelism. Warm, relational, and focused on helping new believers take their first confident steps.</p>\n    <h3>Session Flow</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Session 1: Welcome to the Family — What Just Happened to You (salvation explained)</li>\n      <li>Session 2: Your New Habits — Bible, Prayer, Church, and Telling Someone</li>\n      <li>Session 3: The Church Is Your Family — How to Get Connected</li>\n      <li>Session 4: Your First Step — Baptism, a Discipler, and a Ministry</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Format</h3>\n    <p>4 sessions of 60–75 minutes each, ideally run as a small group (4–8 people) for relational warmth. A personal discipler is assigned before Session 1 begins.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · New Believers Orientation · Runs monthly", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,0,247,'train-bible-reading','Daily Bible Reading Plan','training','manual',false,true,'{"type": "🎯 Training · Level 1 — Team Member", "title": "Daily Bible Reading Plan", "body": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n    <p>The church''s published devotional guide and accompanying reading plan — the daily anchor of every disciple''s spiritual formation. Developed in-house and contextualized for the Filipino believer, with Philippine illustrations, Tagalog-English blend, and local application points.</p>\n    <h3>Structure</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Daily reading:</strong> A passage from the Old Testament, New Testament, and Psalms/Proverbs (using a through-the-Bible-in-a-year plan)</li>\n      <li><strong>Daily devotional:</strong> A 300-word reflection written by church leaders on a rotating basis</li>\n      <li><strong>Daily response:</strong> 3 journal prompts — What did God say? What does it mean for me? What will I do today?</li>\n      <li><strong>Weekly:</strong> A discussion question for Life Community groups</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Accountability</h3>\n    <p>Disciples bring their filled journal to their monthly one-on-one with their discipler. The devotional journal becomes the primary tool for accountability and growth tracking.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Published Devotional Guide · Distributed monthly/quarterly", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,0,248,'assess-discipleship-self','Basic Discipleship Self-Assessment','assessment','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📋 Assessment · Level 0 — New Believer", "title": "Basic Discipleship Self-Assessment", "body": "<h3>Purpose</h3>\n    <p>A simple, honest self-assessment completed by every Team Member at the beginning of each quarter — tracking growth in the core habits of self-leadership. It is not a test to pass but a mirror to look into honestly.</p>\n    <h3>Areas Assessed</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Daily Bible reading: How consistent am I? (Days per week in the last month)</li>\n      <li>Prayer: Do I have a regular, structured prayer time?</li>\n      <li>Journaling: Am I recording what God is speaking?</li>\n      <li>Church attendance: Consistent? Missing when it''s not necessary?</li>\n      <li>Life Community: Am I genuinely engaged or just showing up?</li>\n      <li>EOLO: Have I identified my one person? Am I praying for them?</li>\n      <li>Character: Where am I growing? Where am I struggling?</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Format</h3>\n    <p>A 1-page (front and back) self-assessment form brought to the monthly discipler one-on-one meeting. The discipler does not grade it — they use it as a conversation starter.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Discipleship Self-Assessment · Monthly / Quarterly", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
  (null,0,249,'assess-spiritual-readiness','Spiritual Readiness Inventory','assessment','manual',false,true,'{"type": "📋 Assessment · Level 0 — New Believer", "title": "Spiritual Readiness Inventory", "body": "<h3>Purpose</h3>\n    <p>Completed at the end of BTLI 101, this inventory assesses whether the Team Member has built the foundational spiritual habits that make further growth and ministry participation sustainable.</p>\n    <h3>Readiness Indicators</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Can articulate their personal testimony in 3 minutes or less</li>\n      <li>Has established a daily devotional routine (4+ days/week for 8+ weeks)</li>\n      <li>Has completed all BTLI 101 memory verses</li>\n      <li>Is consistently participating in a Life Community</li>\n      <li>Has made at least one EOLO invitation</li>\n      <li>Has been baptized or has scheduled a baptism</li>\n      <li>Has identified a discipler and is meeting regularly</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Outcome</h3>\n    <p>Completion of this inventory (7 of 7 indicators confirmed) marks the formal completion of the Team Member level and opens the pathway to BTLI 102 and the Leader level.</p>", "footer": "Your Church · Spiritual Readiness Inventory · Completed at end of BTLI 101", "source": "multiply-template"}'::jsonb),
